<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic
        SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="AZD: Project summary, board and list" id="Azd-Boards-Project-Page">

    <primary-label ref="azd"/>
    <show-structure for="chapter,procedure" depth="2"/>

    <link-summary>Open an Azure DevOps project in an editor tab with Summary, Board and List tabs: team charts, a Kanban board with drag and drop, and a list that shows children under their parents.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>Open a project's Summary, Kanban board and List in the IDE, filter by team, and move cards between columns.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>Azure Boards projects in JetBrains IDEs with AZD: a Summary of a team's work, a Kanban board with drag and drop,
        WIP limits and swimlanes, and a List with parent and child hierarchy.</web-summary>

    <p>
        A project page shows the work of one team in an editor tab, with three tabs: <control>Summary</control>, <control>Board</control> and <control>List</control>.
        You can open any project of your organization or collection.
    </p>

    <chapter title="Open a project" id="open-project">
        <secondary-label ref="azd_boards_page"/>
        <procedure id="open-project-proc">
            <step>
                <p>In the <control>AZD Boards</control> title bar, click <control>Open Project…</control>.</p>
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>Type to filter the list, then select a project under <control>Starred</control> or <control>All projects</control>,
                    and press <shortcut>Enter</shortcut> or click it.</p>
                <img src="azd_boards_project_picker.png" alt="Open Project popup with a starred project and the list of all projects" width="566" border-effect="rounded"/>
            </step>
        </procedure>
        <list>
            <li>The project opens in an editor tab named after the project. Opening a project that is already open switches to its tab.</li>
            <li>Click the star next to a project in the popup, or in the page header, to list it under <control>Starred</control>.
                Stars are kept in the IDE on this computer; they are not your Azure DevOps favorites.</li>
            <li>The page opens on the tab you used last for that project, <control>Summary</control> the first time.</li>
            <li>Project pages are not reopened after you restart the IDE.</li>
        </list>
        <p>
            The page header has <control>Refresh</control> and <control>Open in Azure DevOps</control>.
            On the <control>Board</control> tab, <control>Open in Azure DevOps</control> opens that team's board in the browser.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Choose the team and filters" id="team-and-filters">
        <p>
            The first filter of every tab is <control>Team</control>. It starts on the team you chose last for the project,
            otherwise on the project's default team. The <control>Board</control> tab also has a <control>Board</control> filter.
        </p>
        <p>
            Each tab keeps its own filters, and AZD remembers them for each project and team.
            Changing the team clears the <control>Iteration</control> filter.
        </p>
        <p>
            <control>Summary</control> and <control>List</control> show the backlog work items in the team's area paths.
            Completed work items are included only if they changed in the last 31 days, and removed ones are left out.
            The page loads up to 2,000 work items. If the team has no area paths, the page shows the whole project and says so.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Summary" id="summary-tab">
        <p>The <control>Summary</control> tab gives an overview of the team's work.</p>
        <img src="azd_boards_summary.png" alt="Summary tab with the Completed, Updated, Created and Due soon tiles and the Status overview, Recently updated, Types of work and Team workload widgets" width="706" border-effect="rounded" thumbnail="true"/>
        <list>
            <li>Four tiles count the work items <control>Completed</control>, <control>Updated</control> and <control>Created</control> in the
                last 7, 14 or 30 days, and the open ones <control>Due soon</control> in the next 7 days.
                Choose the period in the first filter; it changes only the tiles.
                <control>Due soon</control> uses the Due Date or Target Date field and does not show when the project has neither.</li>
            <li>The widgets show <control>Status overview</control>, <control>Recently updated</control>,
                <control>Types of work</control>, <control>Team workload</control> and, when the project uses Priority,
                <control>Priority breakdown</control>. Click a work item in <control>Recently updated</control> to open it.</li>
            <li>Filter by <control>Assigned to</control>, <control>Type</control> and <control>State</control>.</li>
        </list>
        <p>
            Click the <control>More</control> button (⋯) of a widget to select <control>Show as table</control>, <control>Maximize</control> or <control>Hide</control>.
            Hidden widgets are remembered for the project; click <control>Show widget</control> under the widgets to bring one back.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Board" id="kanban-board">
        <p>
            The <control>Board</control> tab shows the columns, swimlanes and cards of the selected team board.
            A column with a work-in-progress limit shows its count and limit, and its tooltip warns you when the column is over the limit.
            Cards show the fields chosen in the team's card settings, the tags, the state, the assignee and the priority.
        </p>
        <img src="azd_boards_kanban.png" alt="Board tab with Kanban columns, a work-in-progress limit and the Team and Board filters" width="706" border-effect="rounded" thumbnail="true"/>
        <procedure title="Move a card" id="move-card">
            <step>
                <p>Drag the card to another column. AZD changes the work item's state in Azure DevOps.</p>
            </step>
            <step>
                <p>Or right-click the card, select <control>Move to Column</control> and select the column.</p>
            </step>
        </procedure>
        <list>
            <li>A card can't move to a column that has no state for its work item type, or to another swimlane.</li>
            <li>If someone else changed the work item in the meantime, the card does not move and the board refreshes.</li>
            <li>The order of cards inside a column is not saved to Azure DevOps.</li>
        </list>
        <p>
            Filter the cards by <control>Assigned to</control>, <control>Type</control>, <control>State</control>,
            <control>Iteration</control> and <control>Tags</control>, or with <control>Recently updated</control> (the last 7 days)
            and <control>Assigned to me</control>. A column whose cards are all filtered out says how many are hidden.
        </p>
        <p>
            The board shows up to 200 of the most recently changed work items, and up to 100 cards in a column.
        </p>
        <p>Right-click a card, or click its <control>More actions</control> button (⋯), for these actions:</p>
        <img src="azd_boards_card_menu.png" alt="Card menu with Open, Move to Column, Edit Title, Create Branch and Delete Work Item" width="496" border-effect="rounded"/>
        <deflist type="medium">
            <def title="Open">Opens the work item; see <a href="Azd-Work-Item-Details.topic"/>.</def>
            <def title="Move to Column">Moves the card to the column you select.</def>
            <def title="Edit Title…">Renames the work item.</def>
            <def title="Create Branch…">Creates a Git branch for the work item; see <a href="Azd-Work-Item-Branches-Commits.topic" anchor="create-branch"/>.</def>
            <def title="Delete Work Item…">Moves the work item to the Azure DevOps recycle bin after you confirm.</def>
        </deflist>
        <p>
            You can use the board from the keyboard: the arrow keys move between cards and columns, <shortcut>Enter</shortcut> opens a card,
            and <shortcut>Shift+Enter</shortcut> opens its menu.
        </p>
        <note>
            Under Remote Development, dragging cards does not work on the JetBrains Client. Use <control>Move to Column</control> in the card menu instead.
        </note>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="List" id="list-tab">
        <p>
            The <control>List</control> tab shows the work items in a table with the type, ID, title, state, assignee, iteration and update date,
            and the priority when the project uses it. Click a column header to sort.
            Search by title or ID, and filter with the same filters as the <control>Board</control> tab.
        </p>
        <p>
            Child work items are indented under their parents. Use <control>Expand All</control> and <control>Collapse All</control>
            in the toolbar, or click <control>Show Hierarchy</control> to turn the hierarchy off and show a flat list.
            AZD remembers the choice for the project. The hierarchy is not shown while a filter is active.
        </p>
        <img src="azd_boards_list_hierarchy.png" alt="List tab with Show Hierarchy on and child work items indented under their parents" width="706" border-effect="rounded" thumbnail="true"/>
        <p>
            Double-click a work item or press <shortcut>Enter</shortcut> to open it.
            Right-click it to open it on Azure DevOps, copy its URL, create a branch, delete it or refresh the list.
        </p>
    </chapter>

